From af53b31ab88613434bd138a93844e9f5a16607bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:34:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(interaction): retain native held block-use sessions

Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5 retains StartItemUseOn through physical use holds.
Simulation-triggered repeats suppress ordinary block activation. Transport
the control lifetime from aware Java clients, stop on release or capability
withdrawal, and preserve independent uses for ordinary clients.

Match each local prediction to its concluding Java sequence. Prediction
format 2 distinguishes placement, interaction and failure and carries the
native cursor relative to the current target. Native held snapping keeps
the initial world hit even outside later target cubes. Reject non-finite
coordinates and stale sequence ownership without clamping valid positions.
The Java raycast packet remains unchanged for other consumers.

Start the session only after predicted success, retain simulation triggers
after failed attempts, and send the observed first use-on/use-in-air phases
with the original held stack. Native Creative and Survival captures use
empty inventory-action lists. Let the server consume blocks instead of
submitting duplicate slot deltas.

Emit native build/interact swings before successful held transactions.
Java 26.3 uses a local right-click swing, so do not reserve the next PUNCH
packet for it and suppress a later attack. Dropping build swings in a
native relay does not change retained placement facing.

Native and Java Survival both accept server facing corrections when the
camera update precedes placement. Earlier teleport fixtures placed before
the native camera update and cannot establish a server direction lock.
Compare stable-camera ordering rather than forcing an orientation.

Focused tests cover held lifetimes, sequence/result/cursor ownership,
release, failed attempts, ordinary clients and the native block-item phase.
Matching native, direct and proxy fixtures verify authoritative placement
and consumption. Captures and proprietary resources remain private.
